# A PLACEHOLDER, not a validation policy.
#
# The DCAT.Atlas portal reports readiness CRITICAL when its shapes directory is configured but holds
# no *.ttl, on the grounds that validation would then silently pass everything — and the directory is
# configured inside the image, so leaving it unmounted does not help. This file exists only so the
# stack comes up.
#
# The official GovData DCAT-AP.de shapes are AGPL-3.0 and are deployment input: they are not
# vendored here. Replace this file with the set your deployment is required to enforce, and turn
# SHACL_ENFORCE on when you do.
#
# Note that the portal's model-level write floor applies regardless of SHACL — validate-on-write is
# independent of it — so a Catalog still cannot be stored without a publisher Agent and a
# description, nor a Distribution without a licence.

@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix dcat: <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#> .
@prefix dct:  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/shapes/placeholder/CatalogShape> a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass dcat:Catalog ;
    sh:property [ sh:path dct:title ; sh:minCount 1 ; sh:severity sh:Violation ] .
